{#
  view/j-user/users/create.phtml — a new account.

  Same form object as the edit page, primed differently: `setValidatorsForCreate()` adds the
  two uniqueness validators, `setName('create_user')` is what changes the `<form>`'s name and
  id, and a GET pre-selects the four `is_default = 1` roles. See
  JUser\Controller\UserCreateController.

  Three differences from the edit template, all of them the .phtml's:

  - **no `userId` row** — there is no account yet;
  - **`personId` is rendered unconditionally**, where the edit view guards it on the select
    having options at all;
  - **a link to the role form sits between the roles select and the person select**, so an
    administrator who needs a role that does not exist yet can go and make one.

  The `<h1>` translates since 2026-08-21 — see the note in user-edit.html.twig for what it
  used to do and why.

  **These two pages close their `<form>` and the .phtml did not.** Neither `create.phtml`
  nor `create-role.phtml` calls `closeTag()` — they end at `formSubmit()` — so laminas
  serves an unclosed `<form>` that a browser has to close for it at `</body>`, taking the
  footer into the form on the way. Emitting `</form>` is the only other deliberate
  difference in this batch besides the delete page's missing name: every field and the
  submit button are already above it, nothing after it is an input, and an unclosed form
  element is invalid HTML rather than a style choice.
#}
{% extends juser_layout %}

{% block content %}
<h1>{{ translate(page_title) }}</h1>

{{ form_open(form, '') }}
{{ form_row(form.get('username')) }}
{{ form_row(form.get('email')) }}
{{ form_row(form.get('displayName')) }}
{{ form_row(form.get('rolesList'), false) }}
<p><a href="{{ juser_path('juser/create-role') }}">{{ translate('Create new role') }}</a></p>
{{ form_row(form.get('personId'), false) }}
{{ form_row(form.get('isMultiPersonUser')) }}
{{ form_row(form.get('emailVerified')) }}
{{ form_row(form.get('active')) }}
{{ form_row(form.get('security')) }}
{{ form_submit(form.get('submit')) }}
{{ form_close() }}
{% endblock %}
